```yaml
verdict: NEEDS_REWORK
confidence: medium
lenses:
  coverage:
    status: fail
    findings:
      - {gate: G1, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "Gold total is 8400 in the feature but 8500 in AC-3 (15% of 10000). A wrong 16% Gold discount would pass.", location: "features/discount.feature:16"}
      - {gate: G1, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "AC-4 (Bronze, 7 cents, charged 7 cents, rounding in the customer's favour) has no scenario. The plan's claim that every criterion is covered is false.", location: "details/2026-08-13/test.md:12"}
      - {gate: G2, severity: HIGH, finding: "The rounding boundary is not represented, so any rounding direction would pass.", location: "features/discount.feature"}
  business-alignment:
    status: pass
    findings: []
  testability:
    status: fail
    findings:
      - {gate: G9, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "The test copies the wrong Gold value 8400 from the feature.", location: "tests/CheckoutPricing.UnitTest/LoyaltyDiscount/DiscountTests.cs:11"}
      - {gate: G10, severity: BLOCKER, finding: "No production skeleton exists (CalculateLoyaltyDiscount, query, LoyaltyTier, quote). The test fails at compile time, not on a business assertion. I did not run a build, because there are no source projects.", location: "DiscountTests.cs:1-18"}
      - {gate: G6, severity: HIGH, finding: "The impl plan has no per-scenario entries or boundary and does not reference the test file.", location: "details/2026-08-13/impl.md"}
      - {gate: G11, severity: LOW, finding: "The unit-test file exists in the right project. It is not referenced by the plan, and the file name differs from the class name.", location: "DiscountTests.cs:6"}
  boundary-enforcement:
    status: inconclusive
    findings:
      - {gate: G7, severity: HIGH, finding: "contracts-{story}.md is missing, so the entry point cannot be checked against a contract.", location: "test.md:8"}
      - {gate: G8, severity: HIGH, finding: "No walking skeleton is marked.", location: "test.md"}
synthesis:
  questions:
    completeness: {answered_by: [coverage], weight: 0.30, contribution: 0.00}
    business-fit: {answered_by: [business-alignment], weight: 0.30, contribution: 0.30}
    quality: {answered_by: [testability], weight: 0.15, contribution: 0.00}
    risk: {answered_by: [boundary-enforcement], weight: 0.25, contribution: 0.125}
  blocking_findings: ["G1 Gold 8400 vs 8500", "G1 AC-4 has no scenario", "G9 test encodes 8400", "G10 no skeleton, so no business-RED"]
  recommendations: ["Fix Gold to 8500 in the feature and test", "Add an AC-4 scenario", "Add the production skeleton", "Add per-scenario impl entries, a walking skeleton marker and a contracts file"]
  dissent: "Business-alignment passes: the wording is clean. The failures are about values and coverage, not vocabulary. The minority pass is upheld for its own lens and does not offset the blockers."
```

Implementation cannot safely start from this specification. The full-coverage claim is false, and two defects would let wrong behaviour through:
- **Wrong Gold price:** the feature and test expect 8400 cents, but AC-3 says 8500. Implementers would build a 16% Gold discount and the tests would pass.
- **Missing rounding case:** AC-4 has no scenario, so rounding direction is unchecked and rounding against the customer would pass.

The review file is at `.copilot-tracking/skraft-plans/pricing/reviews/2026-10-18/distill-review-1.md`.
